-inline constexpr uint16_t kProtocolVersion = 65003; // custom walkie-radio build // v150 (2026-09-01, THE LIGHT GROUP GETS AN OWNER): + LightGroupState=129, host-authored, KeyedTogglePayload. The shipped light lane synced Alightswitch_C::A -- the switch's PRESENTATION bit (mesh + click), which bytecode shows use() toggles UNCONDITIONALLY while it reaches the lamps only through runTrigger(root,0), gated on the root's `active`. So the switch and the lights are structurally decoupled, `A` is not save-persistent and the group's state is, and nothing on either peer owned or reconciled trigger_lightRoot_C::isActive at all. Host-authored because 13 cooked blueprints can move a group and most are host-owned world systems. No payload changed; a NEW KIND did, so a b149 peer would ignore the lane and silently keep the defect -- hence the bump. v149 (2026-08-31, post-ship audit: the admission blob now covers the challenge's FLAGS byte and the host's own nonce, 126 -> 159 B, tag `multivoid-peer-admission-v1` -> `-v2`. The flag that tells a joiner a password is wanted was OUTSIDE the host's signature, so a relay could set it on an OPEN lobby's challenge and a bound client would derive and emit a real tag to a host that never asked -- turning P1's impersonation residual into a tag-harvesting oracle. No payload size changed; the SIGNED PREIMAGE did, which old builds cannot verify -- hence the bump. v148 (2026-08-31, THE LOBBY PASSWORD IS ENFORCED -- `locked` stops being a badge. `AuthChallengePayload` 96 -> 100 B (+flags u8 +3 pad): the HOST tells the joiner a password is wanted, because a DIRECT or LAN connect has no browser row to infer it from. `AuthProofPayload` 64 -> 100 B (+hasPw u8 +3 pad +pwTag[32]): HMAC-SHA256(K, "MVLP1"||hostPub||clientPub||hostNonce) with K = PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256(password, salt=hostPub, 200k). THE TAG IS A SEPARATE FIELD AND DELIBERATELY NOT IN THE SIGNED BLOB: mixing a KDF of a low-entropy secret into a signature the verifier can recompute is an OFFLINE