tled rig; a per-packet baseline would starve updDirt forever on slow drift): updTires iff mask|types changed (its constraint re-form is measured UNCONDITIONAL -- per-tire conditionality is visibility+collision only, so a bare updTires yields the author-identical rig), updDirt iff fixes changed or a dirt float moved >0.01, updSpareTire iff the spare group changed, updHealth (pure smoke visual) iff |health delta|>0.5; fuel needs NO verb (gauges read per tick) and runout() -- the engine-death verb -- is never called by the sync. tiresValid=0 means the producer could not read its own arrays and the receiver touches NOTHING (mask 0 is the legal all-ejected state, so absence gets its own bit -- the v143 birthLen rule). The idle syncer's change gate gains a condition-block term (a parked host eject must not wait out the 2 s keepalive). battery is deliberately ABSENT: it is an inserted PROP's charge, the prop lane's row. A parse change on both sides, so the bump is mandatory. Prior: v146 (2026-08-29, ATV arc 1 -- a peer that does not author an ATV stops FREEZING it. The mirror model inverts: physics stays ON so the game's own 5-body constraint rig (sus_*/ax_*) runs natively, only the BRAIN is switched off, and the receiver is CORRECTED toward the authority instead of teleported. This is a wire change on BOTH ATV payloads, hence the mandatory bump. `AtvStatePayload` 60 -> 84 B: +linVel[3] +angVel[3], written HARD every packet the way `CNetAPI::ReadVehiclePuresync` writes SetMoveSpeed/SetTurnSpeed, plus a new `authorSlot` that replaces `stateBits` bit3 `authored` -- the boolean said only WHETHER some peer was driving, which was all a receiver needed while its choice was freeze-or-not; with nothing freezing, the question becomes WHO, because `authorSlot == 0xFF` is what elects the HOST as the idle vehicle's syncer (`CUnoccupiedVehicleSync`). `AtvReleasePayload` 56 -> 32 B: the six velocity floats are DELETED, and that deletion is the fix rather than a tidy-up -- `[V]` they were applied to the other peer's copy at the instant its physics was re-enabled, from a pose that had been frozen and was therefore already stale, which the autonomous two-peer probe measured as a 158 cm/s launch that put the client's ATV 109.9 cm away with its rig thrashing at 29.58 cm against a native 2-4 cm band (docs/vehicles/ATV.md 13). There is no un-freeze to inherit a velocity for. `occupantSlot` deliberately STAYS a separate byte from `authorSlot`: it is the SEAT, and `device_occupancy.cpp:230` denies an E-press from it, so fusing them would make a peer merely GRABBING an ATV deny the seat nobody is sitting in. Also in this bump, not on the wire: the seven `BndEvt__*ComponentHitSignature` delegates are cancelled on a non-owner by an authority-gated interceptor [CORRECTED within b146 by `28a958e8`: the guard now NEUTERS -- writes a zero FVector over NormalImpulse and ALWAYS dispatches -- because cancelling the five wheel delegates was itself the 25-40 cm mirror sag (ATV.md 17); kept here as the dated record, see the v147 entry] -- `[V]` they reach `health -= |NormalImpulse|/500000*2*getBumperMult()` and `explode()` at <=0, and they are dispatched by the physics scene, not the tick, so turning physics on without them would let a mirror blow up a vehicle its authority still has. Prior: v145 (2026-08-29, security A59 -- the P2P signaling relay stops believing a name its caller cannot sign for. b144 made a peer's DURABLE public key its rendezvous name, and `[V]` the relay's greeting was `<token> <identity>` with the identity SELF-ASSERTED and the token a static bearer every mod user holds (`signaling.rs:169`), while registration was EVICT-ON-DUPLICATE (`cl.insert`, `:216`) -- so hosting a lobby once harvested the permanent key of every client that joined (it is `m_identityRemote`, handed over as a matter of protocol), and one socket declaring that key thereafter evicted the victim as fast as they re-registered, in EVERY future session. The name could not be rotated