v144 (2026-08-29, security A15/A2/A57 -- a peer is seated only after it PROVES the identity it advertises. Until now the durable player identity was a 32-hex string minted into multivoid.ini and appended to the Join packet, and the host keyed that peer's stored inventory by it: copy the `player_guid=` line and you ARE that player, with a receive boundary that could only check the SHAPE of the name and never the right to it. The identity is now an Ed25519 keypair in multivoid_identity.key, its PUBLIC KEY is the peer's GNS identity, and the guid every store uses is `hex(SHA-256(pubkey)[0..16])` RECOMPUTED BY THE HOST. THREE PARSE CHANGES, hence the mandatory bump: +AuthHello=125 / AuthChallenge=126 / AuthProof=127 (the mutual challenge, host proves itself FIRST), and the Join payload LOSES its [u8 guidlen][guid] field -- the skin/prefs/color tail all shift up by it. THE EXCHANGE IS LOAD-BEARING AND NOT A CEREMONY: `[V]` a GNS cert's `identity_string` and its `key_data` are independent protobuf fields and the library binds NEITHER to the other (`connections.cpp:1452-1458` compares the identity to what the connection expects, `:1497` verifies the session signature against key_data, and nothing compares the two), so a peer CAN present a victim's key as its identity and pass every check GNS makes -- the signature it then cannot produce is the whole control. Neither key is on the wire: each end reads the other's 32 identity bytes off its OWN connection, because a key carried in a payload proves possession of a key the sender chose. There is no fourth message -- `[V]` FinishPeerConnected sends AssignPeerSlot only on a host and only from AdmitPending, so its arrival IS the admission signal, and the client refuses it unless the host has proved itself. Also in this bump: the pending band finally enforces the deadline its own comment has claimed since 2026-08-26 (`pendingSinceMs_` was written at three sites and read at NONE), and a full band now evicts its OLDEST un-proved sock